def find_Max(A,l,r):
    if l > r:
        return -1
    if l == r:
        return A[l]
    mid = l + (r-l)//2
    if A[mid] > A[mid-1] and A[mid] > A[mid+1]:
        return A[mid]
    if A[mid] > A[r]:
        return find_Max(A,l,mid-1)
    return find_Max(A,mid+1,r)
```

The solve the problem of finding the maximum element in a sorted and rotated array, we are using a simple binary search algorithm. In each step of the binary search, we compare the middle element with its adjacent elements to determine whether we are going to the left half (if the middle element is greater than both its adjacent elements) or the right half (if the middle element is smaller than both its adjacent elements). We keep shrinking the search space until we find the maximum element, which is the value at the boundaries or when we explicitly check the endpoints. The solution looks at the central element and compares it with its adjacent elements to decide the direction to continue the search. This ensures that the complete search space is checked effectively.

