In the above code, the function `remove_similar_row` iterates over the matrix to find similar rows. A tuple is considered similar if it has the same length and all elements at the same indices are equal across all rows it's compared to. If similar rows are found, the function is added to a set to avoid duplicates and then at the end of the entire process, the set containing similar rows is returned.

